  "published": "2026-11-18T19:54:03Z",
  "modified": "2026-11-18T19:54:03Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory corruption in HTTP/2 flow control\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-123007.patch: account for frames queued but\n       not yet sent when validating a client WINDOW_UPDATE, so refunding\n       them on stream termination can no longer push the connection send\n       window above NGX_HTTP_V2_MAX_WINDOW\n     - CVE-2026-123007\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free during response processing in resolver\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-123634.patch: release a non-current resolve\n       finalized from another resolve handler through a finalizer instead of\n       reporting it, and report an error to waiting requests when restarting\n       a resolve with a CNAME fails\n     - CVE-2026-123634\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in mail proxy module\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-113425.patch: block client writes while\n       waiting for the auth_http response, while connecting to the upstream\n       and while resolving the SMTP client, discard the queued reply when an\n       auth_http request starts, and switch the client handlers when a\n       session is quitting\n     - CVE-2026-113425\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: buffer overflow with try_files and alias\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-125283.patch: recalculate the length after\n       running the script\n     - CVE-2026-125283\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: endless loop while reading the request body over\n     SSL\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-118899.patch: explicit handling of\n       NGX_AGAIN\n     - CVE-2026-118899\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: ClientHello parsing differential in ssl_preread\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-123640.patch: forbid trailing data in\n       extensions and duplicate SNI/ALPN\n     - CVE-2026-123640",
